--- a/LoongLens/CHANGELOG-v26.md
+++ b/LoongLens/CHANGELOG-v26.md
@@ -0,0 +1,78 @@
+# v26 — v24 baseline, shorter personal routes and faster map handling
+
+This release starts from v24. It uses the original Windows mouse input and
+desktop screenshot capture; the v25 ADB backend is not included. Keep
+BlueStacks visible and focused during Gem Sniping.
+
+## Saved routes
+
+**Edit route → Run route** selects the route that Gem Sniping will run. The
+built-in **Default** is protected. Use **Save as…** to name a variant such as
+**Busy zones**, edit/remove its targets and save. Unsaved changes are protected
+when switching the editor dropdown. A route selector and Save copy button are
+also available on the main Gem Sniping tab.
+
+Each named route retains its own camera positions, extra views and removals.
+The selected route persists across app restarts. Changing routes stops any
+active sniping, waits for input to be released, and resets pass progress, timing
+and find counters. Existing saved v24 edits are imported as **My route** without
+changing the original `camera-route-adjustments.json`. History is shared and kept.
+
+## Remove camera points
+
+In Edit route, select a target and use **Remove selected**. This works for
+original targets and added extra views. Removed targets are skipped in both
+single and repeating passes, with the order and original IDs of the remaining
+points preserved. At least one target must remain.
+
+**Undo remove** restores a removal while the editor is open. **Restore
+originals** reinstates omitted original targets at their default coordinates,
+retaining surviving target adjustments and extra views. **Reset route to
+defaults** restores the complete default route and removes all extras.
+The default exclusions (#26, #51 and #72) remain excluded.
+
+Removing an original target keeps its extra views. Those extras still run and
+can have more extra views added after them. Remove them separately if you want
+to skip their inspections too. Spawn coordinates in the original map/history
+database are not deleted. The editor and Sniping panel show how many listed
+spawn spots are omitted from the personal route. A shorter route may inspect
+fewer locations; it is not equivalent to covering all default spawn spots.
+
+Use **Save & reset checks** to apply the route and clear old pass progress and
+timing. Existing v24 adjustments and extras load automatically as My route.
+Named profiles live under `%LOCALAPPDATA%\LoongLens\routes`; the selection/list
+is in `route-profiles.json`. Profiles with removed originals use format version
+3. The first such save preserves an existing v1/v2 named profile as a
+`.pre-v26.json` sibling. That backup is not overwritten. Routes without removed
+originals continue using version 2, and the original v24 route file is retained.
+
+## Speed changes
+
+- Reuse the just-opened map screenshot for the first alignment observation.
+- Confirm an already recognized map pose against a fresh, nearly unchanged
+  textured frame, avoiding repeated feature extraction. Moving or flat frames
+  still use full recognition. Two observations remain required, and a fresh
+  pre-click screenshot still checks for movement.
+- Avoid an immediate duplicate closed-map screenshot when selection closes
+  the map automatically.
+- Cap the final inspection polling wait at the configured deadline instead
+  of adding an unnecessary full polling interval.
+- Show **Last view**, **Map/load** and **Inspect** times for comparison on your PC.
+
+The default 0.5-second loading wait, 1.2-second empty-view inspection window,
+three-sighting/0.8-second gem confirmation and late-candidate extension are
+unchanged. Focus, obstruction, alignment, portal and F10 guards remain. This
+release does not claim measured live-game speed or detector accuracy on your PC.
+
+`tools/benchmark_sniping.py` verifies all 76 default camera selections against
+independent atlas geometry and reports screenshot/matching counts and timing.
+It uses real atlas pixels with simulated input, loading and empty detection.
+The complete download includes the Windows comparison under `validation/`;
+those numbers are not a live BlueStacks pass.
+
+## Install
+
+Exit the old app completely, extract the complete folder and launch its new
+`LoongLens.exe`. Settings, screenshots and history stay in
+`%LOCALAPPDATA%\LoongLens`; do not delete that directory. The complete 7z contains
+the EXE, source, assets, OCR models, launchers, tests, tools and validation reports.
